From ed402e50abe99604d5a05663cbec31af87f24e18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 10:08:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mixer: Phase 11 patch 0001 -- Shape D mixer-flag
 silence-detect setter

(First patch in patches/SDL_mixer/. Per patch_numbering.md pure-numeric
convention + team-lead 2026-05-12 ACK: slot 0001 is the correct
first-in-series, since patches/SDL_mixer/ was previously empty.)

Surfaces `mixer->actual_mixed_bytes` as a cross-module volatile global
`doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes` so the SDL3-DOS audio backend can
read it in PlayDevice instead of bytewise-scanning the final_mixbuf.
Pairs with patches/SDL/0057 (Shape D reader) and SDL/0058 (Shape A
mechanism histogram). Wave-36 Phase 11 fps lever per
docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md section 4 + team-lead 2026-05-12
no_playing_it_safe.md priority pivot from Shape E -> Shape D
(biggest correctness-retaining ceiling).

Mechanism:

  - MixerCallback (SDL_mixer.c:533+) already tracks
    `mixer->actual_mixed_bytes` internally: line 619-621 sets it to
    the max group_bytes across all groups' tracks for the current mix
    iter. Zero means no track produced any data; non-zero means real
    audio was mixed into final_mixbuf.

  - This patch adds a volatile-int store at the end of MixerCallback,
    just before SDL_PutAudioStreamData, that mirrors the value into
    a cross-TU global. SDL3-DOS PlayDevice can read this in O(1) and
    skip the ring write + SDL_Delay(10) silence-throttle when zero,
    avoiding the per-iter bytewise scan of the staging buffer that
    SDL/0054 Shape A performs.

  - The mixer-bookkeeping value IS the architectural source-of-truth
    for "did this iter produce non-silence" -- the post-mix bytewise
    scan is a redundant re-verification of what the mixer already
    knew. Shape D eliminates the redundancy.

Static-link ordering rationale (DEFINITION lives in SDL_mixer.c, NOT
in SDL3-DOS):

  Doskutsu's nxengine link order is `SDL3::SDL3 SDL3_mixer::SDL3_mixer
  SDL3_image::SDL3_image` per
  vendor/nxengine-evo/CMakeLists.txt:231. With static archives in
  single-pass linker mode, libSDL3.a is processed FIRST; if
  SDL_mixer's reference to the volatile were extern-only and the
  definition lived in SDL3-DOS (SDL_dos_audio_synth.c alongside
  doskutsu_audio_irq_count), the linker would not yet know SDL_mixer
  needs the symbol when processing libSDL3.a, so SDL_dos_audio_synth.o
  might not be pulled in (no other live reference), and SDL_mixer's
  reference would fail to resolve.

  nxengine's existing `doskutsu_audio_irq_count` pattern works because
  nxengine is LAST in the link order -- ld scans prior libs to
  resolve nxengine's externs. Cross-vendor-archive references
  (SDL_mixer -> SDL3-DOS) don't have that luxury without `--start-
  group ... --end-group` flags, which we don't want to require.

  Placing the DEFINITION in SDL_mixer.c (the writer; this patch) and
  the extern decl in SDL3-DOS (the reader; SDL/0057) keeps the link
  single-pass clean: SDL_mixer's TU defines the symbol; SDL3-DOS's
  extern resolves against it.

Workspace-local DOS-port patch per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never
upstreamed. Default behavior unchanged on all non-doskutsu builds:
the extra volatile store is observably a no-op when the SDL3-DOS
reader is not linked in. Cost: 1 volatile-int store per
MixerCallback invocation (~22 Hz at Tier-2 config; ~22 stores/sec).
Negligible.

Strict-"D" engagement: the volatile is READ by SDL3-DOS only when
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_SHAPE=D (env-var-gated; default-OFF;
Shape A bytewise-scan path remains the default). PLAY6 in wave-36
sets SHAPE=D; all other PLAYs run Shape A and ignore this value.

Concurrency / atomicity:

  - Writer: MixerCallback runs on the audio thread under
    device->lock (per SDL3 audio core's SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate
    pattern at SDL_audio.c:1179-1289).
  - Reader: SDL3-DOS PlayDevice runs on the same audio thread under
    the same lock (SDL3 calls GetDeviceBuf -> mix loop ->
    PlayDevice in one critical section).
  - Therefore: same-thread reader; no cross-thread atomicity question.
    `volatile int` for compiler-fence semantics; aligned-int x86
    loads/stores are atomic by ISA anyway. Same pattern as the
    existing `doskutsu_audio_irq_count` / `doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us`
    volatile exports from SDL3-DOS.

Coordination with SDL3-DOS readers:
  - SDL/0057 (Shape D reader): the active consumer. Engaged when
    SHAPE=D.
  - SDL/0058 (Shape A mechanism histogram): does NOT use this
    value; it counts Shape A scan results independently. Both can
    be enabled simultaneously in the same binary; SDL/0057 takes
    precedence in PlayDevice's silence-detect dispatch (Shape D
    path) and SDL/0058 instrumentation rides along the Shape A
    path when SHAPE != D.

Validation:
  - Compile clean at i486 -O3 (visibility-attribute warnings on
    lines 3311+ pre-exist this patch; unrelated to the new code).
  - Symbol `_doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes` verified in
    libSDL3_mixer.a via `strings | grep` after rebuild.

Cross-reference:
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md section 4 + 5.7 (PLAY6 Shape D
    fps lever predicted +3 to +5 fps from 35.71 baseline)
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS.md (the +3.34 ms fi_ms slice
    regression this patch aims to recover)
  - patches/SDL/0057-shape-d-mixer-flag-silence-detect.patch (the
    consumer; SDL3-DOS PlayDevice reads this volatile when SHAPE=D)
  - patches/SDL/0058-shape-a-mechanism-histogram.patch (parallel
    diagnostic backstop; ride-along)
  - memory/no_playing_it_safe.md (2026-05-12 user directive: prefer
    biggest correctness-retaining ceiling over smallest LOC)
  - memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md (rationale
    for the cross-vendor-archive symbol definition placement)
---
 src/SDL_mixer.c | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 58 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/SDL_mixer.c b/src/SDL_mixer.c
index 242d6412..21b10e78 100644
--- a/src/SDL_mixer.c
+++ b/src/SDL_mixer.c
@@ -633,9 +633,67 @@ static void SDLCALL MixerCallback(void *userdata, SDL_AudioStream *stream, int a
         mixer->postmix_callback(mixer->postmix_callback_userdata, mixer, &mixer->spec, final_mixbuf, additional_amount / sizeof (float));
     }
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0001): surface mixer->actual_mixed_bytes
+       as a cross-module volatile global so the SDL3-DOS audio backend
+       (vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c) can read it without
+       a bytewise scan of the final_mixbuf. Pairs with patches/SDL/0057
+       Shape D mixer-flag silence-detect.
+
+       Mechanism: mixer->actual_mixed_bytes is already tracked above
+       (line ~619-621 in vendor source: max group_bytes across all
+       groups). Zero == no track produced any data this iter == mix
+       result is silence. Non-zero == at least one track had data ==
+       PlayDevice should write the mixed buffer to the ring as normal.
+
+       Definition lives HERE (SDL_mixer.c) rather than in SDL3-DOS
+       because of static-link ordering: with the doskutsu link order
+       `SDL3::SDL3 SDL3_mixer::SDL3_mixer ...` (per
+       vendor/nxengine-evo/CMakeLists.txt:231), libSDL3.a is processed
+       FIRST; an extern reference from SDL_mixer to a symbol defined
+       in SDL3-DOS would not be resolved without --start-group
+       linker flags. Placing the definition in SDL_mixer.c (the writer)
+       and the extern decl in SDL3-DOS (the reader) keeps the link
+       single-pass clean. nxengine's existing
+       `doskutsu_audio_irq_count` pattern works because nxengine is
+       LAST in the link order, so ld searches prior libs to resolve
+       it; cross-vendor-archive references don't have that luxury.
+
+       Workspace-local DOS-port patch per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md;
+       never upstreamed. Default behavior unchanged: SDL_mixer
+       continues to operate identically on all non-doskutsu builds;
+       the extra volatile store is observably a no-op when the SDL3-
+       DOS reader is not linked in.
+
+       Cost: 1 volatile store per MixerCallback invocation (~22 Hz at
+       Tier-2 config; ~22 stores/sec). Negligible.
+
+       Strict-"D" engagement: the volatile is READ by SDL3-DOS only
+       when SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_SHAPE=D (see SDL/0057);
+       otherwise Shape A bytewise-scan path runs as before, ignoring
+       this value. */
+    extern volatile int doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes;
+    doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes = mixer->actual_mixed_bytes;
+
     SDL_PutAudioStreamData(stream, final_mixbuf, additional_amount);
 }
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0001): definition of the cross-module
+   volatile that MixerCallback writes above. SDL3-DOS audio backend
+   declares this as extern and reads it in PlayDevice when
+   SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_SHAPE=D engages Shape D (per
+   patches/SDL/0057). Initial value 0 means "silent" -- safe default
+   that won't false-trigger ring writes before the first MixerCallback
+   fires.
+
+   Volatile int chosen (not _Atomic) for DOS DJGPP compatibility +
+   single-writer (audio thread) single-reader (audio thread) cross-TU
+   pattern; semantics match the existing
+   `doskutsu_audio_irq_count`/`doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us` exports
+   from SDL3-DOS (volatile uint32_t with no atomic semantics; x86
+   aligned-int loads/stores are atomic by ISA). */
+volatile int doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes = 0;
+
+
 int MIX_Generate(MIX_Mixer *mixer, void *buffer, int buflen)
 {
     SDL_AudioSpec output_spec;
-- 
